1
00:00:17,016 --> 00:00:18,768
Hey. Victim's name is John Flynn.

2
00:00:18,893 --> 00:00:21,812
He's 48, married... Cho's
bringing the wife now...

3
00:00:21,938 --> 00:00:23,648
And C.E.O. of a company
called Symphony.

4
00:00:23,773 --> 00:00:24,815
Symphony?

5
00:00:24,941 --> 00:00:26,901
Web site says it's a high-end
matchmaking service.

6
00:00:27,026 --> 00:00:28,945
Rich old men looking for hot young chicks?

7
00:00:29,070 --> 00:00:31,906
Yep. Flynn was shot twice
in the chest at close range

8
00:00:32,031 --> 00:00:33,658
then dumped or fell in the water.

9
00:00:33,783 --> 00:00:35,535
A woman heard some pops
from her boat

10
00:00:35,701 --> 00:00:38,329
putting the time of death
at 5:38 P.M. last night.

11
00:00:38,704 --> 00:00:41,123
- Did she see anything?
- No. No witnesses.

12
00:00:42,542 --> 00:00:45,545
- Bruising looks to be a few days old.
- Coroner thought the same.

13
00:00:45,795 --> 00:00:48,297
So far he and forensics haven't
found much else that helps us.

14
00:00:55,888 --> 00:00:58,432
Jane, anything to add before we go?

15
00:00:58,599 --> 00:01:00,935
Yeah, the sun and the sea...
isn't it wonderful?

16
00:01:02,436 --> 00:01:04,021
Anything to add about the victim?

17
00:01:04,438 --> 00:01:07,024
Rich guy, C.E.O.
probably killed over money.

18
00:01:07,191 --> 00:01:09,235
- Way of the world.
- That's all you got?

19
00:01:09,860 --> 00:01:13,614
Do you know in seven years, each and every
cell is completely replaced in your body?

20
00:01:13,990 --> 00:01:17,451
That means you are literally a different
person from when we first met.

21
00:01:18,452 --> 00:01:19,787
Sadder but wiser.

22
00:01:20,580 --> 00:01:21,622
He's very wet.

23
00:01:22,498 --> 00:01:23,833
That must mean something.

24
00:01:40,349 --> 00:01:41,684
- Grieving widow?
- Yeah.

25
00:01:50,067 --> 00:01:51,861
- Hello.
- Hi.

26
00:01:52,945 --> 00:01:55,364
- You were watching me.
- Yes.

27
00:01:56,157 --> 00:01:57,950
- Why?
- It's my job.

28
00:02:01,287 --> 00:02:03,372
Your husband was murdered
at the marina last night.

29
00:02:03,873 --> 00:02:04,915
Yes.

30
00:02:07,877 --> 00:02:10,171
- Sorry for your loss.
- Thank you.

31
00:02:11,464 --> 00:02:14,592
- You seem genuinely upset.
- Does that surprise you?

32
00:02:15,051 --> 00:02:16,510
How long were you
and your husband married?

33
00:02:16,761 --> 00:02:19,263
- I'm sorry. I don't know your name.
- Patrick.

34
00:02:20,473 --> 00:02:23,017
Erica. About a year.

35
00:02:28,814 --> 00:02:29,857
What do you see?

36
00:02:30,232 --> 00:02:32,401
You're independent,
ambitious, competitive

37
00:02:32,568 --> 00:02:34,320
yet you have a warmth about you...

38
00:02:34,654 --> 00:02:39,033
Enough to charm the stoic agent Cho
which is no small feat, let me tell you.

39
00:02:39,867 --> 00:02:42,536
You're skilled at getting people
to open up to you, to trust you.

40
00:02:43,579 --> 00:02:46,165
And there's a question of whether
you use that skill to help people

41
00:02:46,290 --> 00:02:48,209
or to manipulate them.

42
00:02:50,628 --> 00:02:52,630
A little of both, if I'm being honest.

43
00:02:53,673 --> 00:02:56,509
I'm a matchmaker.
I help people find true love.

44
00:02:58,678 --> 00:03:02,598
- You think it's silly.
- No. Good enough job, I imagine.

45
00:03:02,807 --> 00:03:05,393
- You think the idea of true love is silly.
- No.

46
00:03:07,770 --> 00:03:09,730
- That explains it.
- Explains what?

47
00:03:10,314 --> 00:03:12,066
The utter sadness I see in you.

48
00:03:15,653 --> 00:03:17,571
We're all finished, Mrs. Flynn.
I could walk you out, if you like.

49
00:03:17,738 --> 00:03:19,782
Thank you, agent Cho.
You've been very good to me.

50
00:03:20,324 --> 00:03:22,785
- I'll walk her out, if you don't mind.
- Not at all.

51
00:03:23,119 --> 00:03:24,161
Sure.

52
00:03:31,043 --> 00:03:32,503
It was very nice to meet you, Patrick.

53
00:03:32,920 --> 00:03:35,548
Hopefully next time,
it'll be under better circumstances.

54
00:03:38,926 --> 00:03:42,054
You know, every day women come to me

55
00:03:42,430 --> 00:03:45,975
hoping I'll help them find a kind,
gentle man to fall in love with.

56
00:03:47,435 --> 00:03:49,729
I'm sure any one of them
would be lucky to meet you.

57
00:03:56,402 --> 00:03:57,445
What was that all about?

58
00:03:58,070 --> 00:04:00,114
Oh, she's just thanking me
for consoling her.

59
00:04:00,364 --> 00:04:02,950
Oh, and here I thought you
hated talking to widows.

60
00:04:03,492 --> 00:04:06,370
- This one's a little different.
- How so?

61
00:04:07,830 --> 00:04:09,039
She murdered her husband.

62
00:04:22,926 --> 00:04:25,471
You're right. Usually, it's the victim's
spouse who's the murderer

63
00:04:25,596 --> 00:04:27,181
but Erica Flynn has an alibi.

64
00:04:28,265 --> 00:04:29,808
I'd expect nothing less from her.

65
00:04:30,058 --> 00:04:31,727
One of her clients is in
with Rigsby right now

66
00:04:31,852 --> 00:04:34,438
and she swears that she was with
Erica at the time of death.

67
00:04:34,688 --> 00:04:35,731
Then I must be wrong.

68
00:04:36,023 --> 00:04:38,692
She did say that her husband
got in a fight a few days ago

69
00:04:39,193 --> 00:04:40,444
he came home with a bruise.

70
00:04:40,652 --> 00:04:42,821
- She doesn't know who the fight was with.
- Any guesses?

71
00:04:42,988 --> 00:04:45,866
The reality is John Flynn ran
a multi-million dollar company.

72
00:04:45,991 --> 00:04:49,620
He had money, dozens of employees
and a lot of ruthless competitors.

73
00:04:49,787 --> 00:04:53,457
And Flynn's file also says that he gave
half a million dollars to charity last year.

74
00:04:53,916 --> 00:04:55,459
That's the first time
he's ever done that.

75
00:04:55,751 --> 00:04:57,711
- So?
- It's a red flag.

76
00:04:57,836 --> 00:05:01,965
{\an8}- How is giving to charity a red flag?
- Giving to charity isn't a red flag.

77
00:05:02,090 --> 00:05:05,260
{\an8}Giving half a million dollars
to charity, out of the blue, is.

78
00:05:06,053 --> 00:05:07,679
{\an8}It's a sure sign of a guilty conscience.

79
00:05:07,888 --> 00:05:09,348
That is so far from the truth.

80
00:05:09,473 --> 00:05:12,351
{\an8}Well, think about the people that donate
that kind of money to charity...

81
00:05:12,726 --> 00:05:17,231
{\an8}All right, Wall Street executives,
crooked politicians, troubled celebrities...

82
00:05:17,356 --> 00:05:19,691
{\an8}It is all in the name of
clearing their conscience.

83
00:05:19,817 --> 00:05:20,859
You're horrible.

84
00:05:21,902 --> 00:05:23,487
{\an8}How long have you been
a member of Symphony?

85
00:05:24,238 --> 00:05:25,906
{\an8}Oh, just a few days, actually.

86
00:05:26,114 --> 00:05:28,033
{\an8}Night before last was my first
interview with Erica.

87
00:05:28,200 --> 00:05:31,829
{\an8}- And what time was this?
- From 05:00 until just after 6:00.

88
00:05:32,079 --> 00:05:34,289
And you're convinced that Erica Flynn
was there the entire time?

89
00:05:34,414 --> 00:05:36,500
- Yes.
- Can anyone confirm that?

90
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:38,794
{\an8}Oh, I think the rest of the staff

91
00:05:38,961 --> 00:05:40,671
{\an8}had already left the office
by the time we started.

92
00:05:40,796 --> 00:05:43,507
{\an8}I'm a litigator, so that was the
earliest I could meet Erica.

93
00:05:44,132 --> 00:05:46,426
{\an8}Oh, it's probably why I joined
the service in the first place.

94
00:05:46,593 --> 00:05:48,971
{\an8}It's not that I'm some
social leper or anything.

95
00:05:49,096 --> 00:05:51,598
{\an8}I mean, I can meet people.
I meet people all the time.

96
00:05:52,140 --> 00:05:53,433
So... no?

97
00:05:54,893 --> 00:05:55,936
No.

98
00:05:57,145 --> 00:05:58,313
But there's the DVD.

99
00:05:58,564 --> 00:06:00,357
{\an8}- The DVD?
- Of the interview.

100
00:06:00,482 --> 00:06:02,109
{\an8}Yeah, it's part of,
uh, Symphony's service.

101
00:06:02,234 --> 00:06:06,029
{\an8}A client interview, appearance
counseling, date coaching.

102
00:06:06,154 --> 00:06:08,407
{\an8}It's actually a very thorough
approach to matchmaking.

103
00:06:09,283 --> 00:06:13,036
{\an8}Anyway, Erica was interviewing
me the whole time.

104
00:06:13,245 --> 00:06:14,371
{\an8}Just see for yourself.

105
00:06:17,207 --> 00:06:19,710
{\an8}Just... just... God, don't show it
to too many people

106
00:06:19,835 --> 00:06:21,169
'cause it's kind of embarrassing.

107
00:06:21,545 --> 00:06:26,174
{\an8}And they haven't edited out
all my silly faces, dumb comments yet.

108
00:06:26,550 --> 00:06:29,636
{\an8}Oh, my God. Okay, it's fine.
You can watch it.

109
00:06:30,596 --> 00:06:32,723
{\an8}I mean, for investigative
purposes, obviously

110
00:06:32,848 --> 00:06:36,602
{\an8}not that if you wanted to watch it
for other reasons you couldn't.

111
00:06:37,352 --> 00:06:40,147
{\an8}Got it. Uh, well, we'll call
with any other questions.

112
00:06:40,522 --> 00:06:43,817
- Thanks for your time.
- Okay, right. Well, no, thank you.

113
00:06:46,737 --> 00:06:49,573
{\an8}All right, I-I had...
I have a question.

114
00:06:50,949 --> 00:06:52,951
I... will just...

115
00:06:54,202 --> 00:06:56,705
Are you in a relationship?

116
00:06:58,206 --> 00:07:00,751
No. I'm... I'm not, actually.

117
00:07:03,545 --> 00:07:05,631
Well... good to know.

118
00:07:07,466 --> 00:07:11,053
- Uh, nice to meet you, agent Rigsby.
- Nice to meet you, Sarah.

119
00:07:12,512 --> 00:07:13,764
- This way.
- Right.

120
00:07:19,186 --> 00:07:21,563
Hey, boss.
You gotta see this.

121
00:07:22,314 --> 00:07:26,193
It's a video of John Flynn's
ex-wife, Kim Cartwright.

122
00:07:27,277 --> 00:07:28,904
I found it online while doing background.

123
00:07:30,697 --> 00:07:36,662
"3 months ago, my husband of 21 years
John Flynn, told me he was divorcing me."

124
00:07:36,870 --> 00:07:41,291
"John said he wanted to be alone that
he didn't want to be married anymore."

125
00:07:42,042 --> 00:07:44,336
"Well, John, this is what I think
of your settlement agreement."

126
00:07:45,796 --> 00:07:49,091
"Word is out on you, John.
I am going to tell everyone"

127
00:07:49,216 --> 00:07:51,051
"exactly what kind of a man you are"

128
00:07:51,176 --> 00:07:54,096
"because you are a pig!
You are a coward!"

129
00:07:54,888 --> 00:07:58,392
"I made that video over a year ago.
I was upset."

130
00:07:58,642 --> 00:08:00,477
You were more than upset, Ms. Cartwright.

131
00:08:00,811 --> 00:08:02,854
You threatened to make your
ex-husband's life miserable.

132
00:08:03,939 --> 00:08:06,608
Talk to me when your
ex-husband remarries

133
00:08:06,733 --> 00:08:09,236
someone ten years younger
and two sizes smaller.

134
00:08:10,821 --> 00:08:12,698
Libby, no, no. No barking.

135
00:08:13,991 --> 00:08:16,952
- Where were you that night?
- I was home alone.

136
00:08:17,786 --> 00:08:20,038
I didn't kill John,
if that's what you're thinking.

137
00:08:24,418 --> 00:08:27,754
Oh, my God. That's what you're thinking.
That's insane!

138
00:08:28,213 --> 00:08:31,466
John and I reconciled months ago.
We... we spoke all the time.

139
00:08:32,884 --> 00:08:34,386
Including the afternoon he was murdered.

140
00:08:35,220 --> 00:08:36,638
Do you recall what you two talked about?

141
00:08:37,305 --> 00:08:41,351
John was unhappy in his marriage
and he needed someone to listen.

142
00:08:41,476 --> 00:08:44,771
- So he called his ex-wife?
- Okay, it's complicated, all right?

143
00:08:45,272 --> 00:08:48,066
Shh. Shh. Bad dog. Shh. No bark.

144
00:08:50,360 --> 00:08:53,196
You said John was unhappy in his marriage.
Why?

145
00:08:53,655 --> 00:08:54,698
Well, John loved his company

146
00:08:54,823 --> 00:08:57,034
but he was ready
to step back and enjoy life

147
00:08:57,159 --> 00:08:59,494
and Erica didn't feel that way.

148
00:08:59,619 --> 00:09:01,621
She kept pushing him
to expand Symphony.

149
00:09:01,997 --> 00:09:04,332
- It caused problems between them.
- Shh!

150
00:09:08,545 --> 00:09:10,756
When we found John,
he had a bruise over his left eye.

151
00:09:11,006 --> 00:09:15,093
He mentioned that he'd gotten into a fight
with an ex-client, Henry Cliff.

152
00:09:15,302 --> 00:09:18,138
- You know what the fight was about?
- No, he was evasive.

153
00:09:19,056 --> 00:09:20,432
It was something
he didn't wanna share.

154
00:09:20,640 --> 00:09:22,684
Did you know Erica Flynn signed a prenup
before she got married?

155
00:09:22,809 --> 00:09:24,061
You're barking up the wrong tree.

156
00:09:24,269 --> 00:09:26,188
Time stamp puts the start
of the meeting at 5:00 P.M.

157
00:09:26,313 --> 00:09:28,940
It finishes just after 6:00,
just like Sarah said

158
00:09:29,107 --> 00:09:31,151
which means that Erica
Flynn was at her office

159
00:09:31,276 --> 00:09:33,070
- at the time of the murder.
- "Try to look directly into camera."

160
00:09:33,278 --> 00:09:35,489
"It will allow your future soul mate
to better connect with you."

161
00:09:35,822 --> 00:09:37,574
What do you think of these dating
services anyway?

162
00:09:37,741 --> 00:09:39,743
- No and yes.
- What?

163
00:09:40,285 --> 00:09:41,995
No, I've never used
one, and yes, you should.

164
00:09:42,329 --> 00:09:43,789
Oh, because you're cool, and I'm not?

165
00:09:43,955 --> 00:09:45,582
Anything to stop you
dating your co-workers.

166
00:09:46,208 --> 00:09:47,584
"How would your closest
friends describe you"

167
00:09:47,709 --> 00:09:51,797
- "to someone who doesn't know you?"
- "Oh. Well, I think they would say..."

168
00:09:52,547 --> 00:09:55,258
"Uh, we have you scheduled
to come in next Tuesday."

169
00:09:56,635 --> 00:09:58,553
Okay, great. See you then.

170
00:10:00,722 --> 00:10:01,765
Welcome to Symphony.

171
00:10:02,307 --> 00:10:04,726
If you'll just fill out this profile
someone will be with you shortly.

172
00:10:04,976 --> 00:10:06,019
Profile.

173
00:10:06,436 --> 00:10:09,481
Patrick. I see you two have met.

174
00:10:10,232 --> 00:10:12,734
Peter's our reception clerk,
though I doubt for much longer.

175
00:10:12,943 --> 00:10:16,238
He's a very talented musician,
writes such beautiful music.

176
00:10:17,155 --> 00:10:20,617
Patrick is a consultant with CBI.
He's investigating John's murder.

177
00:10:21,701 --> 00:10:22,744
I'll hold your calls.

178
00:10:27,999 --> 00:10:30,168
We're all a little overwhelmed
today, as you can imagine.

179
00:10:30,460 --> 00:10:31,586
I shouldn't even be here.

180
00:10:32,129 --> 00:10:33,755
But to be honest, I didn't
have much of a choice.

181
00:10:33,964 --> 00:10:37,634
With John gone, well, you understand.

182
00:10:38,760 --> 00:10:40,887
- Is there any news in the investigation?
- No.

183
00:10:42,222 --> 00:10:45,308
- Do you have any more questions for me?
- Not really.

184
00:10:47,811 --> 00:10:50,147
- I think I understand.
- Understand what?

185
00:10:51,022 --> 00:10:53,984
Why you're here. I wasn't sure at first
when I saw your ring

186
00:10:54,109 --> 00:10:56,862
- but you're single, aren't you?
- That's not why I'm here.

187
00:10:57,529 --> 00:10:59,072
There's nothing to be ashamed of, Patrick.

188
00:10:59,197 --> 00:11:01,908
I've helped a great many clients
in the exact same situation as you.

189
00:11:02,033 --> 00:11:04,536
Well, I'm not in a situation.
There's no situation.

190
00:11:04,995 --> 00:11:06,872
I know what you're feeling.
I've been there.

191
00:11:07,789 --> 00:11:08,957
Yeah, I don't think you have.

192
00:11:10,375 --> 00:11:12,669
You were in a relationship
once, you were in love

193
00:11:13,211 --> 00:11:15,922
but it ended badly, and you
were deeply hurt as a result.

194
00:11:16,923 --> 00:11:19,259
You shut yourself off from the world
and avoid meeting new people

195
00:11:19,384 --> 00:11:21,928
because you don't want
to ever feel that loss again.

196
00:11:24,764 --> 00:11:26,808
But now you're ready to move on
with your life.

197
00:11:27,684 --> 00:11:28,935
I can see it in you.

198
00:11:29,978 --> 00:11:32,522
You can find happiness
again, even true love

199
00:11:33,565 --> 00:11:35,317
but you have to be willing
to let me help you.

200
00:11:42,073 --> 00:11:44,576
That was spooky.
It was like you read my mind.

201
00:11:46,870 --> 00:11:48,705
Our in-house studio is right this way.

202
00:11:48,872 --> 00:11:50,874
It's where we conduct
our client interviews.

203
00:11:51,249 --> 00:11:52,876
How many interviews
have you conducted here?

204
00:11:53,376 --> 00:11:54,502
Enough to know what I'm doing.

205
00:11:57,797 --> 00:11:59,049
Whoa. That's bright.

206
00:11:59,591 --> 00:12:00,634
Very fancy.

207
00:12:03,762 --> 00:12:06,181
We like to show our clients
in the best possible light.

208
00:12:06,473 --> 00:12:07,974
I thought true love was blind.

209
00:12:08,475 --> 00:12:11,269
We may love with our hearts,
but first we lust with our eyes.

210
00:12:12,270 --> 00:12:13,313
Don't you agree?

211
00:12:14,898 --> 00:12:16,566
If you make yourself comfortable,
we can get started.

212
00:12:17,067 --> 00:12:18,818
- Here? Okay.
- Yeah.

213
00:12:22,197 --> 00:12:23,865
Try to look directly into the camera.

214
00:12:24,074 --> 00:12:26,660
It will allow your future soul mate
to better connect with you.

215
00:12:29,663 --> 00:12:31,331
- "How's that?"
- "Perfect."

216
00:12:32,207 --> 00:12:34,209
"I'm gonna ask you a series
of standardized questions."

217
00:12:34,334 --> 00:12:36,211
"These have been designed
to get at the heart of who you are"

218
00:12:36,378 --> 00:12:37,754
and who you're compatible with.

219
00:12:38,255 --> 00:12:40,215
Try to answer as honestly as possible.

220
00:12:40,590 --> 00:12:42,300
- Ready? Good.
- Yes.

221
00:12:42,759 --> 00:12:45,762
Now, Patrick what kind of woman
are you interested in?

222
00:12:47,889 --> 00:12:49,140
"Rich, quiet blondes."

223
00:12:49,307 --> 00:12:51,184
"No snoring. That's a deal-breaker."

224
00:12:53,270 --> 00:12:55,063
{\an8}We were told you
punched out John Flynn.

225
00:12:55,689 --> 00:12:57,899
{\an8}Yeah, I hit John.

226
00:12:58,775 --> 00:13:00,902
- It was a misunderstanding.
- Who misunderstood what?

227
00:13:01,152 --> 00:13:04,114
- It was nothing, a tiff.
- Two days before he was murdered.

228
00:13:05,991 --> 00:13:07,033
Am I under arrest?

229
00:13:07,158 --> 00:13:09,411
No, you're just a person of interest
at this point a suspect.

230
00:13:09,744 --> 00:13:11,955
Unless you can clear things up
with a simple explanation.

231
