you're using as your alibi...

479
00:26:56,652 --> 00:26:58,737
A faint clicking noise.

480
00:26:59,154 --> 00:27:00,531
Almost mechanical.

481
00:27:01,115 --> 00:27:02,574
Then I figured out what it was.

482
00:27:05,244 --> 00:27:08,247
"How would you describe
yourself to some..."

483
00:27:08,705 --> 00:27:11,917
A simple tape recorder
just like this one.

484
00:27:12,626 --> 00:27:14,336
I knew you weren't
here for the interview.

485
00:27:15,379 --> 00:27:17,256
How could you be?
You're off killing your husband.

486
00:27:17,464 --> 00:27:19,925
But how do we explain
your voice on the DVD?

487
00:27:20,509 --> 00:27:23,929
- This is ridiculous.
- Recording the interview is easy.

488
00:27:24,263 --> 00:27:26,348
After all, you've done hundreds of them.

489
00:27:26,723 --> 00:27:28,433
And once you had the recorder in place

490
00:27:28,559 --> 00:27:31,895
you had plenty of time to leave through
that door, kill your husband

491
00:27:32,146 --> 00:27:34,690
and come back here without
anyone noticing you're gone.

492
00:27:34,857 --> 00:27:38,026
But there is one thing you needed
in order for your plan to work...

493
00:27:39,403 --> 00:27:40,612
an accomplice.

494
00:27:41,113 --> 00:27:42,823
You needed someone to be here

495
00:27:42,948 --> 00:27:45,784
and to play the recorded questions
at the right time.

496
00:27:45,909 --> 00:27:48,120
That's the one loose end you left untied.

497
00:27:49,663 --> 00:27:50,914
That explains it, doesn't it?

498
00:27:53,292 --> 00:27:54,835
Of course there's just one problem.

499
00:28:03,051 --> 00:28:06,930
So if what you're saying is true
I walked out right past my client

500
00:28:07,347 --> 00:28:08,640
in the middle of her interview.

501
00:28:11,143 --> 00:28:12,561
Something she would
have mentioned, huh?

502
00:28:14,980 --> 00:28:16,815
I didn't kill my husband, Patrick.

503
00:28:19,151 --> 00:28:20,277
I do understand.

504
00:28:20,611 --> 00:28:23,572
After all you've been through,
you see evil everywhere.

505
00:28:23,822 --> 00:28:26,200
- I see you.
- Patrick.

506
00:28:27,367 --> 00:28:33,165
You are a kind, clever, wonderful man.
You have so much potential.

507
00:28:34,708 --> 00:28:36,877
But you have to stop
this obsessive behavior.

508
00:28:37,753 --> 00:28:39,046
You need to get a life.

509
00:28:41,340 --> 00:28:42,382
Good night, Erica.

510
00:28:45,177 --> 00:28:46,220
Good night, Patrick.

511
00:28:53,600 --> 00:28:55,101
All you've proven is that Erica Flynn

512
00:28:55,227 --> 00:28:57,604
may have murdered her
husband, not that she did.

513
00:28:58,521 --> 00:29:00,440
Which is why I need to find
her accomplice.

514
00:29:00,565 --> 00:29:02,901
- If there is an accomplice.
- There's no "if".

515
00:29:03,068 --> 00:29:06,196
Yes, there is. We've got other
viable suspects on this thing.

516
00:29:06,363 --> 00:29:08,740
- Like who?
- Like Naomi, for one.

517
00:29:08,865 --> 00:29:12,077
Naomi? She's a greedy opportunist
that hates men.

518
00:29:12,244 --> 00:29:14,788
- She's not a cold-blooded killer.
- We don't know that for sure.

519
00:29:16,456 --> 00:29:19,918
You always say that the simplest answers
usually are the most likely

520
00:29:20,168 --> 00:29:23,255
but it seems like you're coming up
with more and more elaborate scenarios

521
00:29:23,421 --> 00:29:24,714
just to prove that you're right.

522
00:29:25,048 --> 00:29:27,133
Erica killed her husband.

523
00:29:27,676 --> 00:29:31,054
I am 100% sure of it.

524
00:29:31,596 --> 00:29:32,722
I don't get it.

525
00:29:33,431 --> 00:29:34,849
What is it about this woman?

526
00:29:35,308 --> 00:29:36,851
Why are you so obsessed with her?

527
00:29:38,395 --> 00:29:41,106
Because she doesn't think
I'm smart enough to catch her.

528
00:29:42,774 --> 00:29:44,943
- Oh, well, that's a good reason.
- Yeah.

529
00:29:45,068 --> 00:29:46,778
Healthy. Professional.

530
00:29:48,071 --> 00:29:50,365
Uh, just answer me one more thing.

531
00:29:51,032 --> 00:29:53,410
Okay, if Erica Flynn did
murder her husband

532
00:29:53,576 --> 00:29:55,912
how did she leave the room
without her client noticing?

533
00:29:58,748 --> 00:30:00,000
That I don't know.

534
00:30:01,167 --> 00:30:02,294
But I'm working on it.

535
00:30:06,798 --> 00:30:08,049
You're going to jail, Naomi.

536
00:30:08,800 --> 00:30:10,260
Nothing can prevent that
from happening

537
00:30:10,677 --> 00:30:11,970
but you can help yourself out here.

538
00:30:12,137 --> 00:30:13,388
Tell me what you know about John Flynn.

539
00:30:13,513 --> 00:30:15,015
Nothing.
I've never even met him.

540
00:30:15,181 --> 00:30:16,558
Now we both know that's not true.

541
00:30:17,809 --> 00:30:19,227
John Flynn ran Symphony.

542
00:30:19,394 --> 00:30:21,980
He found out you were blackmailing his
clients and confronted you, didn't he?

543
00:30:22,188 --> 00:30:23,565
I never blackmailed anyone.

544
00:30:23,773 --> 00:30:25,567
But we have multiple victims
who claim otherwise.

545
00:30:25,692 --> 00:30:27,527
We have the video camera
you hid in your hotel room

546
00:30:27,736 --> 00:30:28,945
with other victims on it.

547
00:30:30,488 --> 00:30:31,614
You watched that tape?

548
00:30:34,034 --> 00:30:36,536
Did any of those guys
look like victims to you?

549
00:30:36,953 --> 00:30:39,456
They look like John's being
conned by a clever prostitute.

550
00:30:40,415 --> 00:30:41,916
I'm not a prostitute.

551
00:30:42,167 --> 00:30:43,626
Where were you between
the hours of 5:00 and 6:00

552
00:30:43,752 --> 00:30:46,212
- the night of the murder?
- I want my lawyer.

553
00:30:46,838 --> 00:30:48,965
- I've got nothing more to say to you.
- Okay.

554
00:30:50,717 --> 00:30:52,552
But we're waiting on a warrant
to search your apartment.

555
00:30:52,761 --> 00:30:54,387
You talk now, we can make a deal.

556
00:30:55,221 --> 00:30:57,682
We find anything linking you to the murder
all bets are off.

557
00:30:57,807 --> 00:30:58,850
Lawyer.

558
00:31:02,312 --> 00:31:04,397
Uh, yes, Erica interviewed
me from the A.V. room

559
00:31:04,522 --> 00:31:06,274
- but she never left.
- Are you sure?

560
00:31:06,399 --> 00:31:08,318
Yes. She would've had
to walk right past me.

561
00:31:12,655 --> 00:31:13,698
What are you doing?

562
00:31:14,157 --> 00:31:16,618
During your interview do you remember
how bright the lights were in that room?

563
00:31:17,077 --> 00:31:19,746
- Yes.
- Shining right in your face, in fact.

564
00:31:20,372 --> 00:31:21,539
Well, I guess so.

565
00:31:21,956 --> 00:31:23,833
Yes, I once had a job onstage.

566
00:31:23,958 --> 00:31:26,002
I'll never forget how
bright those lights can be.

567
00:31:27,003 --> 00:31:28,338
What does that have to do
with anything?

568
00:31:28,880 --> 00:31:30,882
I'll show you.
Keep your eye on your phone.

569
00:31:34,302 --> 00:31:35,387
What are you doing?

570
00:31:38,056 --> 00:31:39,099
It's gone.

571
00:31:40,642 --> 00:31:41,684
Precisely.

572
00:31:44,062 --> 00:31:47,065
- Hey, is that Sarah still here?
- Why?

573
00:31:47,315 --> 00:31:49,901
Just had a few, follow-up questions
about the investigation.

574
00:31:51,111 --> 00:31:53,446
You're such a bad liar.
She left five minutes ago.

575
00:31:54,155 --> 00:31:55,198
Really?

576
00:31:55,740 --> 00:31:57,200
Just call her up and ask her out.
What's the big deal?

577
00:31:57,575 --> 00:31:59,411
I can't do that.
It's totally unprofessional.

578
00:32:00,328 --> 00:32:02,997
Unless she says yes.
I think she'd say yes.

579
00:32:03,164 --> 00:32:04,416
I mean, she asked me if I was single.

580
00:32:04,749 --> 00:32:05,792
Why would she ask if I was single

581
00:32:05,917 --> 00:32:07,293
unless she wanted me
to ask her out, right?

582
00:32:23,226 --> 00:32:25,937
Sarah, hi. It's, uh,
Wayne Rigsby from CBI.

583
00:32:32,402 --> 00:32:34,821
If you keep up with these visits
I'm gonna have to start charging you.

584
00:32:35,405 --> 00:32:37,157
Oh, this will be the
last one, I assure you.

585
00:32:38,491 --> 00:32:40,618
Have you given up on this nonsense
about me killing my husband?

586
00:32:40,869 --> 00:32:43,496
Nope, not at all. Not one little tiny bit.

587
00:32:43,872 --> 00:32:45,540
Well, then you must have
cracked the case.

588
00:32:45,832 --> 00:32:49,085
Please tell me. I'm curious to know
who this evil accomplice of mine is.

589
00:32:49,294 --> 00:32:51,379
Well, I came by it rather
easily, I must say

590
00:32:51,671 --> 00:32:55,175
after a-a friend got me
thinking on the right path.

591
00:32:55,550 --> 00:32:56,634
Which path is that?

592
00:32:56,843 --> 00:32:59,929
The simplest answer is most
likely the correct one

593
00:33:00,597 --> 00:33:05,018
which means your accomplice is
someone you can easily manipulate...

594
00:33:05,185 --> 00:33:08,855
A man, which is obvious enough
given your physical attributes.

595
00:33:08,980 --> 00:33:10,398
- I'm really getting tired...
- I'm not finished.

596
00:33:11,316 --> 00:33:14,694
He's also young and
impressionable, weak

597
00:33:15,195 --> 00:33:18,198
but above all, someone you can
make fall in love with you

598
00:33:18,490 --> 00:33:22,619
and someone naive enough to believe
that you had fallen in love with them.

599
00:33:22,744 --> 00:33:24,162
Guess who I'm thinking of.

600
00:33:25,455 --> 00:33:28,208
Yes, that's right.
Your assistant Peter.

601
00:33:33,922 --> 00:33:35,465
You have no idea
what you're talking about.

602
00:33:36,883 --> 00:33:38,635
Ah, we'll find out soon enough.

603
00:33:41,179 --> 00:33:42,222
What's going on?

604
00:33:43,640 --> 00:33:45,934
Mrs. Flynn, we'd like you to
come back to the office with us

605
00:33:46,100 --> 00:33:47,268
answer a few questions.

606
00:33:48,061 --> 00:33:49,521
Of course. Anything to help.

607
00:33:57,570 --> 00:33:59,948
How long do you think it'll take
before he tells me everything?

608
00:34:08,456 --> 00:34:11,125
- How you holding up, Peter?
- I'm tired.

609
00:34:12,794 --> 00:34:14,879
Ah, not to worry.
You won't be here much longer.

610
00:34:15,088 --> 00:34:17,090
I know you're not gonna talk,
and I know why.

611
00:34:19,926 --> 00:34:20,969
You're in love with Erica.

612
00:34:22,011 --> 00:34:23,638
No, that's okay.
You don't need to deny it.

613
00:34:23,805 --> 00:34:24,847
I get it.

614
00:34:24,973 --> 00:34:27,559
She's beautiful, she's smart
she's successful.

615
00:34:29,102 --> 00:34:31,854
- Makes you wonder, though, right?
- Wonder what?

616
00:34:33,815 --> 00:34:34,983
What she sees in you.

617
00:34:36,651 --> 00:34:40,113
Apart from her alibi.
I mean, let's be honest here, Peter.

618
00:34:40,238 --> 00:34:41,864
You don't really have that much
to offer her.

619
00:34:42,365 --> 00:34:44,200
- That's not true.
- Oh, so you are having an affair.

620
00:34:44,409 --> 00:34:47,245
- I-I-I did not say that.
- Right.

621
00:34:48,079 --> 00:34:49,330
We're being honest here, Peter.

622
00:34:49,455 --> 00:34:51,791
Deep down, do you really think
that she loves you?

623
00:34:53,376 --> 00:34:55,878
Or are you just kidding yourself
because it feel so nice to be with her?

624
00:34:56,129 --> 00:35:01,217
- No. I love her, and she loves me.
- She was using you.

625
00:35:01,926 --> 00:35:05,138
- She made you an accessory to murder.
- You're wrong.

626
00:35:05,597 --> 00:35:07,015
She got what she wanted from you

627
00:35:07,140 --> 00:35:08,391
- and now she is done with you.
- Stop. Stop saying that.

628
00:35:08,516 --> 00:35:10,977
She doesn't love you, Peter.
She never did.

629
00:35:11,519 --> 00:35:14,105
Now tell me what happened the night
Erica murdered her husband.

630
00:35:15,273 --> 00:35:17,817
She problem told you that
he was abusing her, right?

631
00:35:18,568 --> 00:35:21,571
- Smacking her around, raping her?
- I don't care what you say.

632
00:35:22,238 --> 00:35:23,448
I'm not gonna hurt Erica.

633
00:35:35,251 --> 00:35:36,294
What do we do now?

634
00:35:39,922 --> 00:35:40,965
Jane?

635
00:35:41,090 --> 00:35:42,133
Let him go.

636
00:35:53,519 --> 00:35:56,898
- Hi, Wayne.
- Oh, hey. Wow. You look amazing.

637
00:35:57,023 --> 00:35:58,941
Oh, thanks. So do you.

638
00:36:00,443 --> 00:36:02,111
- Oh, are you ready to go?
- Yeah.

639
00:36:07,950 --> 00:36:09,202
I was hoping you'd call me.

640
00:36:09,327 --> 00:36:11,996
- Yeah, I'm glad I did.
- Me, too.

641
00:36:23,257 --> 00:36:24,342
Hard at work, I see.

642
00:36:27,804 --> 00:36:28,846
What do you want?

643
00:36:29,180 --> 00:36:31,599
I'd like to thank you for having me
brought down here.

644
00:36:32,433 --> 00:36:33,935
That was very courteous of you.

645
00:36:35,269 --> 00:36:36,729
Though I have to admit,
I was a little surprised

646
00:36:36,854 --> 00:36:38,981
your colleagues decided
to simply let me go

647
00:36:39,691 --> 00:36:41,818
you being so certain
of my guilt and all.

648
00:36:42,902 --> 00:36:45,905
Let me guess...
Peter didn't say a word to you?

649
00:36:47,073 --> 00:36:49,242
Maybe now you'll be able
to move past this nonsense.

650
00:36:50,451 --> 00:36:52,537
Let me tell you something...
I will catch you

651
00:36:53,371 --> 00:36:54,831
sooner or later

652
00:36:55,123 --> 00:36:57,375
and I promise you that I will catch you.

653
00:36:57,875 --> 00:37:02,630
Please. If you were capable of catching me
you would have done so by now.

654
00:37:06,676 --> 00:37:07,719
Good-bye, Patrick.

655
00:37:09,220 --> 00:37:11,013
Jane. Jane, we gotta go.

656
00:37:11,264 --> 00:37:13,516
I just got a call from
S.F.P.D. Peter's dead.

657
00:37:15,810 --> 00:37:16,978
He killed himself.

658
00:37:31,991 --> 00:37:33,075
{\an8}Sleeping pills.

659
00:37:33,325 --> 00:37:35,494
{\an8}Coroner found an empty
bottle in the bathroom.

660
00:37:37,246 --> 00:37:42,334
So... sole accomplice in your crime
just went and killed himself.

661
00:37:44,670 --> 00:37:46,213
Fortunately, however

662
00:37:47,256 --> 00:37:48,382
Peter left a letter.

663
00:37:53,637 --> 00:37:56,932
And I'm betting it will tell us
everything we need to know

664
00:37:57,057 --> 00:37:58,976
about the night your husband
was murdered.

665
00:37:59,643 --> 00:38:03,272
You confess now chances are the A.G.'s
office is gonna cut you a deal.

666
00:38:10,488 --> 00:38:12,865
Open it. I don't believe you.

667
00:38:16,619 --> 00:38:17,661
Be my guest.

668
00:38:26,921 --> 00:38:28,798
Yes, it's a bluff.

669
00:38:30,132 --> 00:38:31,842
Honestly, I expected better from you.

670
00:38:32,510 --> 00:38:34,512
Using poor Peter's suicide as a trap?

671
00:38:34,929 --> 00:38:36,722
That's low, immoral, even.

672
00:38:37,640 --> 00:38:39,642
I tried to tell you. I always win.

673
00:38:39,850 --> 00:38:42,102
You might have gotten away
with murder, but you didn't win.

674
00:38:43,771 --> 00:38:44,814
How's that exactly?

675
00:38:44,939 --> 00:38:46,816
No matter what you say, I know the truth.

676
00:38:47,691 --> 00:38:48,901
You cared about Peter

677
00:38:49,735 --> 00:38:52,363
and it was your actions
that drove him to kill himself.

678
00:38:52,488 --> 00:38:55,491
That is something that you will live with
for the rest of your life.

679
00:38:57,993 --> 00:39:00,204
- I'll manage.
- No, you won't.

680
00:39:00,329 --> 00:39:02,206
It'll eat you up from the inside

681
00:39:02,456 --> 00:39:04,542
because you cared
way too much about him.

682
00:39:05,000 --> 00:39:07,044
- You're wrong.
- No, I'm right.

683
00:39:07,211 --> 00:39:09,380
Just like I'm right about
the first time I saw you.

684
00:39:09,547 --> 00:39:13,676
You are an open book to me.
You're transparent, like glass.

685
00:39:13,884 --> 00:39:16,846
If you think for a moment I even
remotely cared about Peter

686
00:39:17,096 --> 00:39:18,180
you're as gullible as he was.

687
00:39:18,305 --> 00:39:20,349
Not just cared. You loved him.
I know it. Can't you see?

688
00:39:20,474 --> 00:39:22,268
- There's nothing you can hide from me.
- You're a fool.

689
00:39:22,393 --> 00:39:24,019
And you're a terrible liar.

690
00:39:24,770 --> 00:39:27,314
You lost, Erica, not just some little game.

691
00:39:27,481 --> 00:39:29,316
- You lost someone you loved.
- I didn't love Peter.

692
00:39:29,441 --> 00:39:31,944
I could care less about him.
He... He meant nothing to me.

693
00:39:32,695 --> 00:39:34,822
Perfect. That's exactly
what I was hoping to hear

694
00:39:34,989 --> 00:39:37,157
rather, that's exactly what I
was hoping Peter would hear.

695
00:39:37,741 --> 00:39:38,784
Peter.

696
00:39:43,414 --> 00:39:44,456
Peter.

697
00:39:47,084 --> 00:39:48,627
Thank God you're here.

698
00:39:49,169 --> 00:39:51,547
Don't listen to a word they say.
They're telling you lies.

699
00:39:51,881 --> 00:39:53,924
You know how I feel about you, darling.

700
00:39:54,800 --> 00:39:57,511
Peter. Peter! Please!

701
00:39:58,554 --> 00:40:00,097
By the way, there
was a body in that bag.

702
00:40:00,222 --> 00:40:01,974
It wasn't Peter's. No, of course not.

703
00:40:02,141 --> 00:40:04,351
That's kind of obvious.
It was your husband's.

704
00:40:05,352 --> 00:40:09,106
And I told you I would
catch you, and I did.

705
00:40:12,109 --> 00:40:14,153
Erica left ten minutes into the interview.

706
00:40:15,821 --> 00:40:17,990
She told me to wait
behind with the recorder.

707
00:40:20,159 --> 00:40:22,745
"She said if I just played the questions"

708
00:40:23,078 --> 00:40:25,539
"then no one would ever know
she was gone."

709
00:40:29,043 --> 00:40:31,670
She knew John was going down
to the marina after work.

710
00:40:32,504 --> 00:40:33,547
That time of day

711
00:40:33,672 --> 00:40:35,466
there aren't a lot of
people around, you know?

712
00:40:37,593 --> 00:40:39,136
"She waited for him and..."

713
00:40:46,602 --> 00:40:47,686
"And you shot him."

714
00:40:51,774 --> 00:40:54,276
You shot your own husband
in cold blood.

715
00:40:55,611 --> 00:40:56,946
Peter told us everything.

716
00:40:58,155 --> 00:41:02,618
You used him as your accomplice
because he was weak, unstable.

717
00:41:03,410 --> 00:41:05,704
You could manipulate him.
But it backfired.

718
00:41:06,330 --> 00:41:08,832
He couldn't take the pressure
and now he'll testify against you

719
00:41:08,999 --> 00:41:11,835
and you will spend a very
long time in prison.

720
00:41:12,670 --> 00:41:13,796
Don't count on it.

721
00:41:15,631 --> 00:41:16,674
It's over.

722
00:41:17,967 --> 00:41:19,593
A jury still has to believe him.

723
00:41:21,512 --> 00:41:24,723
And he is, as you so
accurately put it, unstable.

724
00:41:25,724 --> 00:41:28,686
Erica, it's over.

725
00:41:29,228 --> 00:41:30,270
I'm sure of it.

726
00:41:31,230 --> 00:41:32,272
Don't be.

727
00:41:33,816 --> 00:41:35,567
Not everyone's as smart as you.

728
00:41:37,569 --> 00:41:38,612
"Jane?"

729
00:41:40,948 --> 00:41:41,991
You in here?

730
00:41:46,328 --> 00:41:48,288
Ah, there's my laptop.

731
00:42:01,635 --> 00:42:05,097
"Uh, I'm looking for someone
who, uh..."

732
00:42:06,598 --> 00:42:09,601
"Someone... I can trust"

733
00:42:10,561 --> 00:42:12,312
"someone strong, someone..."

734
00:42:13,564 --> 00:42:15,065
"At peace with themselves"

735
00:42:15,941 --> 00:42:17,276
"someone better than me"

736
00:42:18,736 --> 00:42:20,195
"someone who knows the..."

737
00:42:22,072 --> 00:42:23,949
"Worst side of me and still loves me."

738
00:42:27,786 --> 00:42:29,204
"Sounds like an amazing woman."

739
00:42:31,331 --> 00:42:32,374
"She was."

